From: Antoine Pirrone <antoine.pirrone@pollen-robotics.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wq_wlan: report the disconnection on a failed roam

rwnx_rx_sm_disconnect_ind() skips cfg80211_disconnected() when the firmware
leaves the old AP as part of a reassociation. If that reassociation then
fails, rwnx_rx_sm_connect_ind() reports only the failed connect result, which
cfg80211 takes to mean "still on the old AP": wdev->connected stays true while
ssid_len is cleared. From then on every NL80211_CMD_CONNECT gets -EALREADY and
cfg80211_disconnect() never reaches the driver (it only calls it when
ssid_len is set), so the link is gone until the module is reloaded.

Seen on the microduck beta board against a multi-AP Livebox: wpa_supplicant
roams within the ESS, the AP answers status 30, and wlan0 never reassociates.
Reproduced on demand with wpa_supplicant's D-Bus Roam() method.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Antoine Pirrone <antoine.pirrone@pollen-robotics.com>
---
diff --git a/src/wifi/rwnx_drv/rwnx_msg_rx.c b/src/wifi/rwnx_drv/rwnx_msg_rx.c
index 2dc1956..bc54b28 100644
--- a/src/wifi/rwnx_drv/rwnx_msg_rx.c
+++ b/src/wifi/rwnx_drv/rwnx_msg_rx.c
@@ -1493,6 +1493,25 @@ static inline int rwnx_rx_sm_connect_ind(struct rwnx_hw *rwnx_hw,
 						req_ie, ind->assoc_req_ie_len,
 						rsp_ie, ind->assoc_rsp_ie_len,
 						ind->status_code, GFP_ATOMIC);
+			/*
+			 * A failed roam: rwnx_rx_sm_disconnect_ind() does not
+			 * report the old AP's disconnection when it is part of a
+			 * reassociation, so cfg80211 still holds that link. A
+			 * failed reassociation leaves cfg80211 believing it is
+			 * still connected, with ssid_len cleared, and from then
+			 * on every connect gets -EALREADY and every disconnect
+			 * is a no-op, until the module is reloaded. The firmware
+			 * has left the old AP: say so.
+			 */
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 1, 0)
+			if (wdev->connected)
+#else
+			if (wdev->current_bss)
+#endif
+				cfg80211_disconnected(dev,
+						      WLAN_REASON_UNSPECIFIED,
+						      NULL, 0, true,
+						      GFP_ATOMIC);
 		}
 		rwnx_hw->connect_req_ts = 0;
 	}
